  "content": {
    "text": "CONCLUDED\nLast Updated:\n7 hours ago\nApple Stock Edges Down. What Was ‘Lacking’ in Its Big AI Announcement.\nApple shares were edging down early on Tuesday as investors digested its artificial-intelligence plans, which raised some questions among analysts.\nApple stock was down 0.3% at $300.74 in premarket trading. The stock had been as much as 3.3% higher on Monday before it unveiled new Apple Intelligence features during its WWDC conference.\n“We found AAPL's WWDC AI updates to be lacking in the context of what we thought was generally a high bar for advancements of Apple Intelligence,” wrote KeyBanc analyst Brandon Nispel. “We saw: no clear signs of monetization of AI; Apple's reliance on Google Gemini; very few use cases where Apple App integration was materially beneficial; and a slightly better standalone Siri, which is still worse than other LLMs [large language models].”",
